          en: ["Correct.", "<b>Wrong:</b> if there is no signal, a more flexible model memorises the noise better; here the forest is even worse than the linear model.", "Correct.", "<b>Wrong:</b> this experiment used only past returns at a daily horizon. With other information (interest differentials, macro data) and longer horizons the result may differ; but the famous Meese–Rogoff (1983) finding shows that is very hard too."]
